codemap 9
tour promote
kind flow
author ai
group cli
note The scaffolding command, and the reason building a flow is not tedious. promote turns a symbol's call tree into a tour shaped like it: one step per symbol, each under the step it is called from, named after the root symbol. By default the tree is pruned (Index::pruned_tree) by rules measured against the hand-written feature tours of this repo: on its CLI features a depth-2 pruned tree kept 85% of the steps the authors chose at 69% precision, where the whole depth-2 tree kept 93% at 20% (TODO item 7's 42-step scaffolds). The result is still a draft, not an answer: the agent then deletes the steps that do not belong to the workflow, re-parents anything the resolver placed wrong, and writes the notes. Running it again on the same tour adds only the symbols the tour does not already have, so a tour can be deepened after a change.

